    "result_text": "The build passes cleanly (exit 0; `-q` suppresses the BUILD SUCCESS line). The change is complete and the full suite is green (64 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors).\n\n## Summary\n\nI redesigned the owner identity key so `identityKey = SHA-256 hex over (normalizedTelephone + '|' + lowerEmail + '|' + soundex(lastName))` and made it the single source of duplicate detection.\n\n**New file**\n- `Soundex.java` \u2014 standard American Soundex encoder, shared by the identity key and the soft-match.\n\n**Changed files**\n- `OwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 `identityKey(telephone, email, lastName)` now returns the lowercase-hex SHA-256 over `normalizedTelephone|lowerEmail|soundex(lastName)` (previously plaintext `telephone|email|householdId`).\n- `RequireUniqueOwnerIdentity.java` \u2014 the 409 duplicate check now keys off `lastName` (soundex, via the new identity key), still skipping the owner itself and soft-deleted owners. The disposable-email blocklist still runs earlier in the pipeline.\n- `AssignPossibleDuplicate.java` \u2014 soft-match now triggers when the full `identityKey` **differs** but `soundex(lastName)` **and** `postcode` match (earliest matching id wins). A declared `sharesHousehold` member is still never flagged.\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 removed the separate `requireHousehold` (household-duplicate 409) step; `assignHousehold` now flows straight to the single `identity` check. `householdId` is still computed for size/level rules.\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 identityKey mapping now passes `owner.getLastName()`.\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 updated the `identityKey` description and example to the new 64-hex SHA-256 form.\n\n**Behavioural effect** (matching the specs and tests):\n- Cp10 \u2014 same lastName + postcode, different telephone \u2192 created as a soft match, no longer a 409.\n- Cp35 \u2014 soft match now fires on soundex(lastName) + postcode with a differing key.\n- Cp28/Cp52 \u2014 identityKey is 64-hex; a full-identity repeat still 409s.\n- Cp03/Cp25 \u2014 exact identity repeats still collide (409); household-only collisions no longer do.\n\n`RequireUniqueOwnerHousehold.java` and its escalation remain in the tree but are no longer wired into the create pipeline (its `normalize` helper is still used by `AssignHouseholdId`).",
